== Notes ==

* ''Spell focus'' does not apply to spells that are granted as special abilities.
* After player chooses ''[[Greater Spell Focus]]'' of the same spell school, the chosen ''Spell Focus'' will be replaced by the greater version and disappear from the Feats list.
* Spontaneous casters ([[bard]]s and [[sorcerer]]s) can take this feat without being able to cast first level spells as long as their [[class level]] qualifies for at least 0 level one spell slots (that is, even if their casting ability is too low to actually cast a level one spell).

==Builder notes==

'''Item feat:''' Yes, except [[transmutation]] (which can be added with custom content).

==Custom content notes==

'''Removable:''' yes

'''Reusable:''' yes

'''Script:''' hardcoded

*''Spell focus'' in transmutation can be added to [[iprp_feats.2da]] to get the missing spell school as an item property.
*A custom class must have this feat in their feat list, or that class will not be able to select it as a general feat.
